=head1 NAME

git-bz - Git integration with Bugzilla for Koha development

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    git bz apply [options] <bug-ref> [bug-ref ...]
    git bz attach [options] [<bug-ref>] <commit-range>
    git bz create [options]
    git bz edit [options] (<bug-ref> | <commit> | <revision-range>)
    git bz info --fields [--refresh]
    git bz open <bug-ref>

=head1 DESCRIPTION

A Perl rewrite of git-bz for Koha development workflow using Bugzilla's REST API.
Provides seamless integration between Git and Bugzilla for patch management.

=head1 COMMANDS

=over 4

=item B<apply>

Apply patches from a Bugzilla bug to the current Git branch.

=item B<attach>

Attach Git commits as patches to a Bugzilla bug.

=item B<create>

Submit a new bug report to Bugzilla. Prompts interactively for required fields
(product, component, version, severity, summary, description) unless they are
supplied via options. Supports C<--dry-run> to check for duplicates without
creating the bug, C<--non-interactive> for scripted use, and C<--json> to emit
machine-readable output.

=item B<edit>

Edit bug details and add comments through an interactive editor.  Pass
C<--non-interactive> together with field options (C<--status>, C<--comment>,
C<--patch-complexity>, C<--sponsorship>, C<--sponsor>, C<--depends>,
C<--assignee>, C<--qa-contact>, C<--obsolete>) to update a bug without
opening an editor, suitable for scripted use.

=item B<info>

Discover valid Bugzilla field values. Use C<--fields> to list available
products, components, and versions as JSON. Results are cached locally for one
week; pass C<--refresh> to force an immediate update from Bugzilla.

=item B<open>

Open bug in default web browser.

=back

=head1 CONFIGURATION

    # Set default Bugzilla tracker
    git config bz.default-tracker bugs.koha-community.org

    # Set credentials via environment
    export BUGZILLA_USER=your-email@example.com
    export BUGZILLA_PASSWORD=your-password

